  "term": "phenylketonuria",
  "definition": "Phenylketonuria is a recessive genetic disorder in which the body cannot properly metabolize and use the amino acid phenylalanine. It can lead to intellectual disability, developmental delay, and behavioral, movement, and seizure problems.",
